IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`
IMPORT `lhl-rules`
IMPORT `lhl-seat`
IMPORT `lhl-seat-host`
IMPORT `lhl-seat-worker`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- worked cases for the host's questions (lhl-seat-host.l4), and the mirror cases:
-- the same facts asked from the provider's, the host's and the worker's seats, with answers that agree. Every expected value
-- was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `host cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`recruitment` MEANS `a business of providing recruitment or placement services`
`other business` MEANS `another business`
`supply` MEANS `wholly or principally the supply of labour`
`placing` MEANS `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person`
`9(1)` MEANS `a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it`
`9(2)(a)` MEANS `a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them for the work`
`s 15 item` MEANS `s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider`
`s 16(2) item` MEANS `s 16(2) entering into an avoidance arrangement`
`s 16(3) item` MEANS `s 16(3) not reporting an avoidance arrangement`

§§ `ss 7 to 10 -- is it labour hire`

#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 15 -- using an unlicensed provider`

-- Arguments: labour hire, provider licensed, provider on the Register, other reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(2)(a): on the Register as a licence holder, though not licensed in fact (finding 4).
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 16 -- avoidance arrangements`

-- Arguments: supply of an individual, supplier on the Register with a licence in force, knows or suspects.
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to enter the avoidance arrangement` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to enter the avoidance arrangement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to enter the avoidance arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to enter the avoidance arrangement` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(3): aware on 1 December 2026, 5 days reasonably practicable: by 6 December 2026.
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 TRUE (`d` 6 12 2026) (`d` 10 12 2026) EQUALS `reported in time`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 TRUE (`d` 7 12 2026) (`d` 10 12 2026) EQUALS `not reported as soon as reasonably practicable (s 16(3))`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 6 12 2026) EQUALS `not yet reported, and still in time`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 7 12 2026) EQUALS `not reported as soon as reasonably practicable (s 16(3))`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 0 TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) (`d` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `reported in time`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `s 16 does not apply: no duty to report`
#ASSERT `Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 12 2026) 5 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `no duty to report yet: you have not become aware of, or suspected, an avoidance purpose`

§§ `s 95 -- involvement`

#ASSERT `Am I treated as a contravener because I was involved` `I aided, abetted, counselled or procured it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a contravener because I was involved` `I conspired with others to contravene it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a contravener because I was involved` `I was not involved in any of these ways` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 46 -- the provider's licence`

#ASSERT `Must the provider show me its licence as a host` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the provider show me its licence as a host` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Penalties and time limits`

#ASSERT `What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` `s 15 item` FALSE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` `s 15 item` TRUE EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT `What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` `s 16(2) item` TRUE EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT `What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` `s 16(3) item` FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` `s 16(3) item` TRUE EQUALS 800
-- s 93(6): 3200 > 2500 for a company: Supreme Court only; 200 <= 500 for an individual: either court.
#ASSERT `Can a host be ordered to pay a civil penalty` `s 15 item` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, by the Supreme Court only (s 93(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can a host be ordered to pay a civil penalty` `s 16(3) item` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, by the Magistrates' Court or the Supreme Court (s 93(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can a host be ordered to pay a civil penalty` `s 15 item` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 2 7 2032) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the application was not made within 6 years of the contravention (s 93(7))`
-- s 93(7): from 29 February 2028, the sixth anniversary falls on 28 February 2034 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Until when can the Authority pursue me as a host` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 7 2032
#ASSERT `Until when can the Authority pursue me as a host` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2034

§§ `Mirror cases: provider, host and worker on the same facts`

-- A business supplies two farmhands it employs and pays to a grower (s 7(1)).
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `9(1)` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Unlicensed: the provider breaks s 13, the host s 15(1), and the worker's question agrees.
#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Licensed: none of the three is told of a contravention.
#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to use this provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A recruitment agency placing staff whom the host pays, without arranging accommodation: not labour hire in any seat.
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my arrangement for labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The licence must be shown to a host and to a worker alike (s 46).
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `a host` EQUALS `Must the provider show me its licence as a host` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `a worker for a provider` EQUALS `Must my provider show me its licence` TRUE
